{"files": [{"path": "CWE401_Memory_Leak__malloc_realloc_int64_t_01.c", "content": "#include "std_testcase.h"

#include <wchar.h>


void CWE401_Memory_Leak__malloc_realloc_int64_t_01_bad()
{
    {
        int64_t * data = (int64_t *)malloc(100*sizeof(int64_t));
        if (data == NULL) {exit(-1);}

        data[0] = 5LL;
        printLongLongLine(data[0]);

        int64_t * temp = (int64_t *)realloc(data, (130000)*sizeof(int64_t));
        if (temp != NULL)
        {
            data = temp;
            data[0] = 10LL;
            printLongLongLine(data[0]);
            free(data);
        }
        else
        {
            free(data);
        }
    }
}
"}], "explanation": "The original code overwrote the only pointer to the malloc'd buffer with realloc's result; if realloc failed (returned NULL), the original buffer leaked. By storing realloc's result in a separate temp pointer, we can free the original buffer on failure while preserving identical output on success."}
